[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Entry points** — there is exactly **one** public entry point, and it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   also the lowest-level one: `encode_base64(int size, const char *src)`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`c_src/include/lib.h:1`). `encode()` is `static`, so it is not reachable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   across the ABI; it is exercised *only* indirectly, which is why axis **V**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   below deliberately drives all five of its branches through crafted bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Runtime options / modes / flags** — the library has **no** setters, **no**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   global or thread-local state, **no** `#ifdef`s and **no** enums. The single
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   mode switch is line 37: `size == 0` reinterprets `src` as a NUL-terminated
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   string (axis **M**).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **M (length mode)**: `M0` = `size == 0` (strlen mode) · `M+` = `size > 0`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (explicit length) · `M-` = `size < 0` (loop skipped).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **R (size mod 3)**: `R0` / `R1` / `R2` — selects the padding branches
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (lines 69/75): `R0` → no `=`, `R1` → `"=="`, `R2` → `"="`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **G (group count)**: `G1` = one 3-byte group · `G2` = two · `Gn` = many.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **V (byte-value class, drives `encode()`)**: `V<26` (`A`–`Z`) · `V26-51`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`a`–`z`) · `V52-61` (`0`–`9`) · `V62` (`+`) · `V63` (`/`) · `Vhigh` = bytes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ≥ 0x80 (negative `signed char` on x86-64, converted to `unsigned char`) ·
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `Vnul` = embedded `0x00` · `Vall` = the full 0..=255 range.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * No byte-order / element-width / format axis exists — the API is byte-oriented.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
